        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c4_speed_asks_what_spend_almost",
          "text": "SPEED asks: what if we spend almost none of the storage budget on a shared dictionary and per-image sparse codes, and let a small network reconstruct rich images from them? That reframing is where the gains come from.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "speed",
            "asks",
            "what",
            "spend",
