          "chunk_id": "s07_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s07_c2_pruning_sparse_coding_matrix_just",
          "text": "Pruning each sparse coding matrix to just forty-eight non-zero elements, about three hundred thousand parameters, meets the storage budget while keeping ConvNet accuracy at seventy-three point five percent, barely below the seventy-four percent of the full fifteen-million-parameter model.",
